[0.000, "o", ".html\u001b[m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\n  (\u001b[34;4m\u001b]8;id=jk6b3c5e42a7046bb4;file:///Users/brett/Documents/GitHub/nuttxspace-egm/tutorial/reference/nuttx-rp2350-driver-traps.md\u0007tutorial/reference/nuttx-rp2350-driver-traps.md\u001b[m\u001b]8;;\u0007)\u001b[K\r\n  • \u001b[1mVerification & CLI Cheat Sheet\u001b[m: \u001b[34;4m\u001b]8;id=jk3ce2620367642d26;file:///Users/brett/Documents/GitHub/nuttxspace-egm/tutorial/reference/verification-and-cli-cheatsheet.html\u0007tutorial/reference/verification-and-cli-cheatsheet.html\u001b[m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\n  (\u001b[34;4m\u001b]8;id=jkfd8767eb255d609d;file:///Users/brett/Documents/GitHub/nuttxspace-egm/tutorial/reference/verification-and-cli-cheatsheet.md\u0007tutorial/reference/verification-and-cli-cheatsheet.md\u001b[m\u001b]8;;\u0007)\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\n  \u001b[1m### Modern Web Guidance\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[K\n  • \u001b[94mdark-mode\u001b[m: I declared \u001b[94m<meta name=\"color-scheme\" content=\"dark\">\u001b[m in \u001b[94m<head>\u001b[m and applied \u001b[94mcolor-scheme: dark\u001b[m on \u001b[94m:root\u001b[m\r\n  (with a \u001b[94m@media print\u001b[m override to \u001b[94mcolor-scheme: light\u001b[m) so viewport scrollbars and native controls match the dark\u001b[K\r\n  theme wit"]
[0.000, "o", "hout flashes (\"Apply the \u001b[94mcolor-scheme\u001b[m property to the \u001b[94mhtml\u001b[m element or the \u001b[94m:root\u001b[m pseudo-class.\").\u001b[K\r\n  • \u001b[94mcustomize-scrollbar-color-and-thickness\u001b[m: I paired \u001b[94mscrollbar-color\u001b[m with \u001b[94mscrollbar-width: thin\u001b[m on \u001b[94m:root\u001b[m and\r\n  scrollable code/table containers to ensure custom scrollbars render on macOS, and gated \u001b[94m::-webkit-scrollbar\u001b[m\r\n  fallbacks behind \u001b[94m@supports not (scrollbar-color: auto)\u001b[m (\"Wrap legacy fallbacks in an \u001b[94m@supports not (scrollbar-\u001b[m\r\n  \u001b[94mcolor: auto)\u001b[m block to prevent conflicts between standard properties and legacy WebKit selectors in browsers that\r\n  support both natively.\").\u001b[K\r\n  • \u001b[94mcross-document-transitions\u001b[m: I enabled multi-page view transitions inside \u001b[94m@media (prefers-reduced-motion: no-\u001b[m\r\n  \u001b[94mpreference)\u001b[m via \u001b[94m@view-transition { navigation: auto; }\u001b[m so navigating between lessons respects motion preferences\r\n  (\"Both the source and destination pages must opt-in to view transitions for the bro"]
[0.000, "o", "wser to trigger them on\u001b[K\r\n  navigation.\").\u001b[K\r\n  • \u001b[94mbrand-consistent-forms\u001b[m: I set \u001b[94maccent-color: var(--accent-color)\u001b[m on \u001b[94m:root\u001b[m with a high-contrast sky-blue token\r\n  (\u001b[94m#38bdf8\u001b[m) and added a \u001b[94m@supports not (accent-color: var(--accent-color))\u001b[m fallback for verification checkboxes (\"You\r\n  MUST use the \u001b[94m@supports not\u001b[m rule to apply custom fallback styles only when \u001b[94maccent-color\u001b[m is not supported.\").\u001b[K\r\n  • \u001b[94maccessibility\u001b[m: I structured every page with semantic landmarks (\u001b[94m<header>\u001b[m, \u001b[94m<nav>\u001b[m, \u001b[94m<main>\u001b[m, \u001b[94m<article>\u001b[m, \u001b[94m<footer>\u001b[m),\r\n  \u001b[94m<th scope=\"col\">\u001b[m table headers, a \u001b[94m.visually-hidden:where(:not(:focus-within, :active))\u001b[m skip link targeting \u001b[94m<h1\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n  \u001b[94mid=\"main-heading\" tabindex=\"-1\">\u001b[m, \u001b[94m:focus-visible\u001b[m outlines with \u001b[94moutline-offset: 2px\u001b[m, and separate \u001b[94mkeydown\u001b[m (\u001b[94mEnter\u001b[m) /\r\n  \u001b[94mkeyup\u001b[m (\u001b[94mSpace\u001b[m) handlers on margin-note triggers (\"When implementing a custom keyboard han"]
[0.000, "o", "dler for button-like\u001b[K\r\n  elements, En\u001b[K\n\n\n\n\u001b[12D\u001b[?2026l"]
